<BaseLayout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure"
  description="FTC affiliate disclosure for HomeBillCuts, including Amazon Associates placeholder language."
  canonicalPath="/disclosure/"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Affiliate Disclosure</h1>
    <p><em>Last updated: September 7, 2026</em></p>

    <div class="callout callout--disclosure">
      <strong>In plain English</strong>
      Some links on HomeBillCuts may be affiliate links. If you buy through them, we may earn a
      commission. It does not change the price you pay. We still try to recommend products and
      approaches that make sense for bill-first energy decisions — and we do not guarantee savings.
    </div>

    <h2>FTC disclosure</h2>
    <p>
      In accordance with the Federal Trade Commission’s guidelines concerning the use of endorsements
      and testimonials in advertising, HomeBillCuts wants you to know that some links on this site
      are affiliate links. This means we may receive compensation if you click a link and purchase a
      product or service. We only use affiliate relationships where we believe the product is relevant
      to the guide’s topic.
    </p>

    <h2>Amazon Associates (placeholder)</h2>
    <p>
      <!-- Replace this paragraph after you are accepted into Amazon Associates. -->
      HomeBillCuts is a participant in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program, an affiliate
      advertising program designed to provide a means for sites to earn advertising fees by
      advertising and linking to Amazon.com. (Placeholder — confirm enrollment and update wording
      as needed for your account and region.)
    </p>

    <h2>How we handle recommendations</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We prioritize no-cost and low-cost actions before product purchases.</li>
      <li>We disclose affiliate relationships near product recommendations in posts.</li>
      <li>We do not invent tracking IDs, fake reviews, or guaranteed dollar savings.</li>
      <li>Affiliate placeholders in content use <code>{'{{AFFILIATE:...}}'}</code> tokens until real links are added.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>Email <strong>hello@homebillcuts.com</strong> or see <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
